chapter.p:
I lie down and sleep in peace,
for you alone, O Lord,
make me feel safe and secure.

In the Lord I take refuge.
How, then, can you say to me,
“Flee to the mountains like a bird;

Upon the wicked, he will rain
coals of fire and brimstone;
a burning blast will be their lot.

For the Lord is righteous;
he loves justice.
The upright will see his face.

who look down on evildoers
but highly esteem God’s servants;
who at all cost stand by a pledged word,

I keep the Lord always before me;
for with him at my right hand,
I will never be shaken.

Then the earth reeled and rocked;
the foundations of the mountains shook;
they trembled at his fury.

This God – his way is perfect;
the word of the Lord can stand fire.
He is a shield for those who seek refuge in him.

Thrusting them through,
I do not give them time to rise;
they fall under my feet.

He delivers me from my foes;
he exalts me above my adversaries;
he rescues me from violent people.

“He has given victories to his king;
he has shown his love to his anointed ones,
to David, and to his descendants forever.”

Now I know that the Lord saves his anointed;
he has answered him from his holy heaven
with victories from his right hand.

The voice of the Lord is over the waters;
the God of glory thunders,
the Lord thunders over vast waters.

Your hand day and night lay heavy upon me;
draining my strength, parching my heart
as in the heat of a summer drought.

So let the faithful ones pray
to you in time of distress;
the overflowing waters will not reach them.

You are my refuge;
you protect me from distress
and surround me with songs of deliverance.

The Lord protects him, preserves his life,
and gives him happiness in the land;
he yields him not to the will of his foes.

My soul is downcast when I remember
from these lands of Jordan and Hermon,
“Where are you, small mountain?”

Make justice, O God, and defend my cause
against an ungodly people;
deliver me from the wicked and deceitful.

Send forth your light and your truth;
let them be my guide,
let them take me to your holy mountain,
to the place where you reside.

Your arrows are sharp, O king,
they pierce the hearts of your enemies;
nations fall beneath your feet.

You love righteousness and hate wickedness;
therefore God, your God, has anointed you
with the oil of gladness, above your fellow kings.

Let Mount Zion rejoice,
let the villages of Judah be glad,
for your justice prevails.

Their graves are their eternal homes,
from generation to generation,
no matter how big the tracts of land they own.

God is no longer silent, he comes;
before him is a devouring fire,
around him a raging storm.

You take no pleasure in sacrifice;
were I to give a burnt offering,
you would not delight in it.

He alone is my rock and salvation;
with him as my stronghold,
I shall not be overcome.

He alone is my rock and my salvation;
with him as my stronghold,
I shall not be overcome.

Trust in him at all times, my people;
pour out your hearts before him;
God is our refuge.

O God, you are my God, it is you I seek;
for you my body longs and my soul thirsts,
as a dry and weary land without water.

By your strength the seas were calmed;
you lull their roaring waves
and the turmoil of the nations.

May God be blessed!
He has not rejected my prayer;
nor withheld his love from me.

May grain abound throughout the land,
waving and rustling as in Lebanon;
may cities teem with people, as fields with grass.

Praised be his glorious name forever;
may the whole earth be filled with his glory!
Amen. Amen.

My flesh and my heart waste away
for you, O God, O my rock,
you are mine forever.

But as for me, my joy is to be near God;
I have made the Lord my refuge,
and I will proclaim all his works.

You called in distress, and I saved you;
unseen, I answered you in thunder;
I tested you at the waters of Meribah.

Without knowledge and understanding,
they walk about in darkness;
all the earth’s foundations are shaken.

Between friends we speak of Egypt and Babylon;
and also Philistia, Tyre, Ethiopia:
“Here so-and-so was born.”

When they call to me, I will answer;
in time of trouble I will be with them;
I will deliver and honor them.

The Lord reigns, robed in majesty;
the Lord is girded with strength.
The world now is firm, it cannot be moved.

Your decrees can be trusted;
holiness dwells in your house
day after day without end, O Lord.

He is our God, and we his people;
the flock he leads and pastures.
Would that today you heard his voice!

For forty years they wearied me and I said,
“They are a people of inconstant heart;
they have not known my ways.”

You who love the Lord, hate evil,
for he preserves the lives of his faithful,
he delivers them from their foes.

Bless the Lord, my soul!
Clothed in majesty and splendor;
O Lord, my God, how great you are!

you build your upper rooms above the waters.
You make the clouds your chariot
and ride on the wings of the wind;

The fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom;
prudent are those who live by his precepts.
To him belongs everlasting praise.

They have hands but cannot feel,
feet, but cannot walk;
neither can they make a sound in their throat.

The Lord remembers us and will bless us;
he will bless the family of Israel;
he will bless the family of Aaron;

He has freed my soul from death,
my eyes from weeping,
my feet from stumbling;

Alleluia!
Praise the Lord, all you nations;
all you peoples, praise him.

Like swarms of bees they encircled me;
but like burning thorns they died down;
in the name of the Lord I crushed them.

Like a bird our soul escaped
from the snare of the fowler;
the snare was broken and we were freed.

I have quieted and stilled my soul
like a weaned child on its mother’s lap;
like a contented child is my soul.

May my tongue cleave to my palate
if I remember you not,
if Jerusalem is not the first of my joys.

Your eyes saw the course of my days;
they were all recorded in your book
before any of them came to be.

I cry to you, O Lord;
I say, “You are my refuge,
my portion in the land of the living.”

Not sooner his spirit has left,
that he goes back to the earth;
on that very day, any plan comes to nothing.

maker of heaven and earth,
the sea and all they contain.
The Lord is forever faithful;

But he sends his word and melts the snow;
he makes his breeze blow,
and again the waters flow.

Alleluia!
Praise God in his sanctuary;
praise him in the vault of heaven.
